# mtk/mt6895/drivers/usb/conf: the MT6895's USB device port.
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_<NAME>=y in a defconfig builds a driver into the kernel (docs/drivers-config.md). MediaTek's drivers are
# `default n`: a configuration has them only when it includes mt6895.config.

driver MT6895_USB
	file    bsd/dev/hakios.mt6895_usb.c
	default n
	help    the USB device port of the Redmi Note 11T Pro (xaga): the MT6895's MTU3 controller at 0x11201000 with its
	help    IPPC block at 0x11203e00 and the port 0 USB2 phy (mediatek,xsphy) at 0x11e40000 (usb=2). Nothing in this
	help    tree had a USB stack -- no bsd/dev/*usb*.c, no iokit usb, no usb header in xnu/files -- so this is written
	help    against Linux drivers/usb/mtu3/, against the phone's own LK (which is a complete, working MTU3 device-mode
	help    implementation: it is what fastboot runs), and against the shape of the sweet port's XNU usb patches.
	help    It starts by reading the state LK left behind rather than resetting it, the way hakios.ufshc.c inherits
	help    LK's task list
